<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Appendix</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Full Results</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the tables below are the full results for our perplexity experiments, for all baseline perturbations (<span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">NO PERTURB</span>, <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">HOP baseline</span>, <span id="A1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">REVERSE baseline</span>) and impossible perturbations (<span id="A1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SHUFFLE global</span>, <span id="A1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SHUFFLE local</span>, <span id="A1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">REVERSE partial</span>, <span id="A1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">REVERSE full</span>, <span id="A1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SWITCH</span>, <span id="A1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">HOP</span>). Metrics for the <span id="A1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">interlinguistic perspective</span> experiment were computed based on these values. AUC was computed with NumPy’s composite trapezoidal rule function <span id="A1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">np.trapz</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>License Compliance</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this study, we utilize datasets from the <span class="ltx_ref ltx_ref_self">Colorless Green RNNs</span> project, which are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution–NonCommercial (CC BY-NC) license. Additionally, we adopt aspects of the methodology described in Kallini et al. (2024), whose <span class="ltx_ref ltx_ref_self">code</span> is available under the MIT License. Both the datasets and the methodological framework are duly cited in the main text.</p>
</div>
</section>
